{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"topics\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Empirical Evidence as a Compiler Optimization Signal\",\n      \"structure_type\": \"wiki\",\n      \"sections\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Shared Evidence Model\",\n          \"body\": \"Both sources treat compiler optimization as an evidence-guided decision problem. The profile-guided source uses execution counts and weighted flow graphs to focus classic C optimizations on frequently executed regions, while the machine-learning source uses empirical training data and learned models to choose optimization heuristics for unseen programs.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Profiles and Learned Models\",\n          \"body\": \"The profile-guided work grounds decisions in runtime counts and reports measured speedups for super-block optimizations. The machine-learning work generalizes empirical evidence into models that predict optimization choices from program features and separates learning from deployment inside the compiler.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Limits of Evidence\",\n          \"body\": \"A synthesis page should compare profile counts, supervised labels, feature values, and performance measurements as related optimization evidence while noting that learned compiler models depend on the quality, cost, and representativeness of their training data.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"claim_ids\": [\n        \"claim-execution-profiles-integrated-into-an-optimizing-c-compiler-can-guide-classic-op--20be52b7603e\",\n        \"claim-weighted-flow-graphs-expose-hot-paths-by-attaching-execution-counts-to-basic-blo--49c47f8431d5\",\n        \"claim-on-the-benchmark-suite-profile-based-super-block-optimizations-averaged-a-1-15-s--e5d7486c0e56\",\n        \"claim-machine-learning-based-compilation-can-use-a-model-inside-the-compiler-to-choose--f8131a5c483d\",\n        \"claim-the-machine-learning-compiler-workflow-separates-model-learning-from-deployment--a04ee1ab9738\",\n        \"claim-supervised-learning-for-compiler-optimization-learns-correlations-between-progra--217abf25c992\",\n        \"claim-machine-learning-based-compilation-can-make-compiler-optimization-more-evidence--20aeeff3a32c\",\n        \"claim-machine-learning-based-compiler-optimization-is-limited-by-the-quality-represent--f9c7d385cc26\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"source-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\",\n        \"source-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Program Representation Choices Shape Optimization Opportunities\",\n      \"structure_type\": \"wiki\",\n      \"sections\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Representation Before Optimization\",\n          \"body\": \"The sources share a concern with how programs are represented before optimization decisions are made. The profile-guided source reshapes hot control-flow paths into super-blocks and super-block loops, while the machine-learning source represents programs through quantifiable static, dynamic, or combined features.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"What Optimizers Can See\",\n          \"body\": \"Super-block formation makes frequently executed paths easier for classic scalar optimizations to exploit. Feature engineering, feature selection, and dimension reduction make program behavior and structure available to learning algorithms without overwhelming models with redundant or sparse feature spaces.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Structural and Statistical Views\",\n          \"body\": \"The topic should preserve the distinction between structural compiler regions and statistical feature vectors, but can synthesize them as representation layers that determine what an optimizer can observe, compare, and act upon.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"claim_ids\": [\n        \"claim-super-blocks-represent-frequently-executed-paths-as-linear-basic-block-sequences--7bbb510c9bb0\",\n        \"claim-trace-selection-followed-by-tail-duplication-converts-frequently-executed-traces--1483ee9d0534\",\n        \"claim-classic-scalar-optimizations-can-be-reformulated-to-operate-on-super-blocks-and--79ce55378df0\",\n        \"claim-program-features-provide-the-quantifiable-representation-that-allows-learning-al--a254f7b701be\",\n        \"claim-feature-selection-and-dimension-reduction-are-necessary-in-compiler-learning-pro--ecd12a4a4f1f\",\n        \"claim-future-research-in-machine-learning-compilation-extends-beyond-choosing-optimiza--faf587f1fc17\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"source-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\",\n        \"source-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Context-Dependent Optimization Tradeoffs\",\n      \"structure_type\": \"wiki\",\n      \"sections\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"No Universally Best Optimization\",\n          \"body\": \"Both sources emphasize that optimization choices are context dependent rather than universally beneficial. Profile-based classic optimizations target hot paths and complement conventional optimization, while machine-learning examples such as thread coarsening depend on program and hardware context.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Competing Objectives\",\n          \"body\": \"The profile-guided work manages tradeoffs such as executable-size growth while seeking speedups. The machine-learning work highlights tradeoffs among parallelism, register pressure, memory behavior, instruction-level parallelism, code size, speed, and power.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Evidence for Payoff Decisions\",\n          \"body\": \"This topic can frame compiler optimization as selecting transformations under competing objectives, with profiling inputs, benchmark measurements, and learned predictions used to identify when a transformation is likely to pay off.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"claim_ids\": [\n        \"claim-profile-based-classic-optimizations-are-intended-to-complement-conventional-opti--6bcefbcf9607\",\n        \"claim-the-profile-based-transformations-controlled-executable-size-growth-averaging-1--5bacab4b8a28\",\n        \"claim-the-experiments-used-separate-profiling-inputs-and-performance-measurement-input--ee5ac2fa5a94\",\n        \"claim-machine-learning-based-compilation-can-use-a-model-inside-the-compiler-to-choose--f8131a5c483d\",\n        \"claim-thread-coarsening-decisions-are-context-dependent-because-coarsening-can-improve--4878860bda89\",\n        \"claim-direct-prediction-of-the-best-compiler-option-is-practical-for-relatively-small--fe68da808ef3\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"source-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\",\n        \"source-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"From Hot-Path Mechanisms to Learned Optimization Policies\",\n      \"structure_type\": \"wiki\",\n      \"sections\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Mechanisms for Exposing Hot Paths\",\n          \"body\": \"The profile-guided source provides concrete mechanisms for exposing and optimizing hot paths: trace selection, tail duplication, eliminating entries into the middle of traces, and focusing optimization on frequently executed loop paths.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Policy Learning Still Needs Compiler Machinery\",\n          \"body\": \"The machine-learning source describes a broader policy-learning view in which models predict optimization decisions from program features, but it also states that learning cannot invent legal transformations or derive legality analyses by itself.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"Connecting Mechanism and Policy\",\n          \"body\": \"A synthesis page could connect hand-engineered hot-path transformations with learned policies: profiles and features can guide when to apply transformations, while compiler-provided legality checks and transformation machinery remain necessary.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"claim_ids\": [\n        \"claim-tail-duplication-creates-additional-optimization-opportunities-because-it-can-ma--6c81300e0307\",\n        \"claim-the-major-effectiveness-mechanisms-are-eliminating-entries-into-the-middle-of-tr--4bc0ff5e21b0\",\n        \"claim-the-implementation-cost-of-profile-based-classic-optimization-was-modest-relativ--062df22ec16c\",\n        \"claim-supervised-learning-for-compiler-optimization-learns-correlations-between-progra--217abf25c992\",\n        \"claim-machine-learning-based-compiler-optimization-is-limited-by-the-quality-represent--f9c7d385cc26\",\n        \"claim-future-research-in-machine-learning-compilation-extends-beyond-choosing-optimiza--faf587f1fc17\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"source-01-using-profile-information-to-assist-classic-code-optimizations--219edcf6f0cf\",\n        \"source-02-machine-learning-in-compiler-optimization--5fbaa9c3f69d\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"}}
